<p class="para lt-chem-349761" id="av_1.0-ch17_s01_s01_p05">Solubility products are determined experimentally by directly measuring either the concentration of one of the component ions or the solubility of the compound in a given amount of water. However, whereas solubility is usually expressed in terms of <em>m</em></p>

<p class="para lt-chem-349761"><em>ass</em> of solute per 100 mL of solvent, <em>K</em><sub>sp</sub>, like <em>K</em>, is defined in terms of the <em>molar</em> concentrations of the component ions.</p>

