    <div class="answer">
    <p class="para lt-chem-349761">22.4 mg; a secondary reaction occurs, where OH<sup>&minus;</sup> from the dissociation of the salt reacts with H<sup>+</sup> from the dissociation of water. This reaction causes further dissociation of the salt (Le Chatelier&rsquo;s principle).</p>
